"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative led by Marcus Cole, launching in Q3 2023 with a kickoff meeting on July 15th. The project aims to enhance security and accessibility, leveraging AI for data visualization and real-time analytics. Key milestones include the approval of a $2M budget (later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses), the completion of the design phase, and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. The team is expanding with five new cybersecurity and cloud architecture specialists, with onboarding scheduled for September 10th. Development is led by Omar Jensen, and a $15,000 training budget has been approved for coding teams and project managers. The next phase involves UI enhancements starting in October."
